## Reviewer got wrong (not applied)
- a#21 and the verdict line that Western grouping of one lakh and above should become lakh figures. Part b says the Western comma is not a fix row when the digits match. ACCEPTED-ROUND and R14 skip lakh/crore grouping because the checker cannot parse it. The pinned token is TWD 1.57M, not a reformatted 15,70,000.
- a#32. Q16–Q20 are body text in the Korean source, and the blank lines are U+200B on purpose. Promoting them to ## headings, or deleting the ZWSP lines, fails headings or blocks. The same applies to b#11.
- a#41. The English table is Difficulty | Easy | Difficult | Easy. The Tamil value cells were already எளிது | கடினம் | எளிது. The first cell is the row label, not a fourth result. Economic dismissal is the Difficult cell; resignation is the last Easy cell. Those values match the English. Only the label was wrong (an adjective where the source is the noun “Difficulty”). Deleting the row would also fail the table-row check.
- b#26’s suggested heading still says முதலீட்டு மறுஆய்வுத் துறை. Part a#25 is the glossary decision: மறுஆய்வு is an appeal or a second look. The heading now says the subsidiary undergoes முதலீட்டு ஆய்வுத் துறை review (உட்படும்), which is the English “undergo”, not “pass”.
